.TH AGENT-WORKFLOW-INDEX 1 "2026-08-02" "agent-workflow 0.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-workflow-index \- rebuild and query the host-local SQLite evidence projection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-workflow index status
.br
.B agent-workflow index sync
.RI [ --run " AGENT_RUN" ]
.RI [ --active-only ]
.br
.B agent-workflow index rebuild
.RI [ --run " AGENT_RUN" ]
.RI [ --active-only ]
.br
.B agent-workflow index verify
.RI [ --full ]
.RI [ --review " AGENT_RUN" ]
.br
.B agent-workflow index query
.I KIND
.RI [ FILTERS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The index command maintains a host-local SQLite projection over authoritative JSON, JSONL, immutable workflow snapshots, and sealed receipts. The database is disposable and reconstructable. It is never launch, lifecycle, workflow, permission, remediation, review, acceptance, merge, or deletion authority.
.PP
One locked indexer owns writes. SQLite uses WAL mode, full synchronous durability, foreign-key enforcement, a bounded busy timeout, and a versioned schema. Queries use fixed parameterized views; the CLI does not expose arbitrary SQL.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Report database path, schema and application versions, journal mode, source/indexed run counts, last synchronization, freshness, and index errors.
.TP
.B sync
Incrementally reconcile changed active and archived run directories. Use
.B --run
for one Agent Run or
.B --active-only
to exclude archived evidence.
.TP
.B rebuild
Remove and recreate the selected projection from authoritative source evidence. A full rebuild also replaces WAL and shared-memory companions. Rebuilding does not alter source artifacts.
.TP
.B verify
Run SQLite integrity and foreign-key checks. With
.B --full,
rehash every indexed source artifact and report missing, changed, or mismatched evidence.
With
.B --review,
also verify one named sealed reviewed run and its direct completion and lifecycle gate evidence; this adds
.B review_valid
without changing the global
.B valid
result.
.TP
.B query
Query one curated read-only view. JSON output is an agent-workflow/index-query/v1 envelope containing projection freshness, stale/error counts, and rows. Human output prints the freshness summary before the table. Supported kinds are
.BR runs ,
.BR incidents ,
.BR permissions ,
.BR performance ,
.BR workflows ,
.B workflow-nodes
and
.BR errors .
.SH QUERY FILTERS
.TP
.B --agent-run AGENT_RUN
Limit results to one Agent Run where the selected view supports it.
.TP
.B --state STATE
Filter run, incident, permission, or workflow state where supported.
.TP
.B --category CATEGORY
Filter incident or index-error category.
.TP
.B --executor NAME
Filter runs or performance observations by executor.
.TP
.B --model MODEL
Filter runs or performance observations by model.
.TP
.B --pack PACK
Filter run or workflow ownership by prompt-pack ID.
.TP
.B --limit N
Bound returned rows.
.SH AUTHORITY AND PRIVACY
Every indexed source retains relative path, record sequence where applicable, schema identity, size/metadata, and SHA-256 provenance. Raw prompts, terminal bodies, message bodies, output logs, credentials, and unrestricted provider payloads are excluded. A query result must be reopened against original evidence before any authority-changing action.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/agent-workflow/index/agent-workflow.sqlite3
Default rebuildable SQLite projection.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/agent-workflow/index/index.lock
Exclusive indexer writer lock.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/agent-workflow/runs/
Active authoritative run evidence.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/agent-workflow/archive/
Archived authoritative run evidence.
.SH RECOVERY
A missing or corrupt database is recovered with:
.PP
.nf
agent-workflow index rebuild
agent-workflow index verify --full
.fi
.PP
A corrupt or unverifiable current source run is recorded as an index error; it is not translated, rewritten, or silently repaired. A valid sealed run with a failed executor result, invalid or missing completion, failed budget policy, or non-pass score remains indexed with separate typed outcome fields and is never treated as accepted merely because it is queryable.
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-workflow(1), agent-workflow-workflow(1), docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/OPERATIONS.md
